From 7e9067fceab28074be72dcde8ef17ee1d9c4ceb4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chiro <chiro2001@163.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 00:27:55 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 114/235] feat(pypto-x): add W8A8 binding schema v2 and packed
 layout v2

Contract 0002 C2 (qwen35-w8a8-binding):
- BINDING_SCHEMA_VERSION 1 -> 2: optional BindingEntry.quant mapping
  (nine frozen keys, per_group/BF16-scale fail closed), quant_scale role,
  from_dict/validate with dangling scale_entry and unknown-key rejection,
  metadata-driven quantized_parameters construction in build_binding_schema.
- PACKED_LAYOUT_VERSION 1 -> 2: every quantized weight expands to
  <param>.int8 (quant_weight) + <param>.scale (quant_scale) regions;
  v1 schema is rejected with reject_and_recompile. BF16 path keeps its
  exact 368-region layout.
- qwen35_decoder_exact_parameter_manifest / expand_decoder_parameter_manifest
  expand the trusted compact manifest into the 320 exact names shared with
  runtime_binding.
- Coverage manifest: w8a8_linear_coverage and
  whole_net_int8_compute_ratio, with 150/186 default coverage and a
  documented static shape MAC model.
- R7-R9 focused tests plus a metadata-only 518-region driver.

No backend kernels, lowering, runtime execution or BF16 schema semantics
were changed.
